comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-03T09:18:32.635Z",codex-toolchain-1103,"Reproduced both reported action tests on the actual 2026.10.30 pin. Neither reaches policy admission: fixture client.create rejects parent:\"none\" with --parent must not use placeholder token none; use --unset parent. Root cause: pm-cli 2026.10.30 GH-1614 typed SDK data stays literal. Classification: test and packed-acceptance fixture contract drift. Replace absent parent/sprint/release with typed unset, and clear assignee using unset during matrix reset (literal none is now a real assignee). Preserve explicit parents in positive controls. Apply the same correction to follow-through fixtures and packed scenarios; retain all native policy/parity assertions, then rerun them to detect any independent admission change."
  "2026-11-03T09:55:50.416Z",codex-toolchain-1103,"Validation so far: npm test -- --test-concurrency=2 builds and typechecks the test graph after correcting the literal field fixture types. Native retained-ownership admission passes through pm test; explicit start roles, close roles, policy advisories, workflow authority, partial-record capability refusals and competing-writer checks also pass. The 120-case severity matrix reaches its existing 600000ms deadline; the full command-option matrix reaches 180000ms on both Node and Bun; the 500-sequence property reaches 300000ms. No deadlines or assertions were widened. Memory-backed temporary trackers and disabled provenance probes are diagnostic runs only; neither is evidence of a passing matrix yet. The original refusal is confirmed GH-1614 parent:none at fixture create, not a changed policy decision. Full exact-head acceptance remains a CI requirement."
  "2026-11-03T10:06:10.753Z",codex-toolchain-1103,"Final bounded npm receipt: 420 reported tests, 407 pass, 1 assertion failure and 12 canceled, zero skips. The assertion failure was the existing future-date activity window, now fixed and independently passing under pm-brief-yanp. The admission severity and option matrices and the 500-sequence property reached their original deadlines; other queued or active files were canceled when the bounded run stopped. Bun focused admission also timed out; memory-backed trackers and disabled provenance probes did not establish a passing matrix. Retained-ownership native admission and the corrected window pass through pm test. Typecheck, build:test, docstring and changelog check pass. No lint script exists. No full suite, packed acceptance, coverage or release:check pass is claimed. All literal sentinel fixture and packed scenario updates are retained, with native parity assertions unchanged."
